its products through specialty distributors, retailers, pool builders, and buying groups. Hayward Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1925 and is headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin P. Holleran | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $573K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue falling 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $116K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Hayward Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.4B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 48%.","The business throws off $227M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.69\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"